# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  KANIDA.AI  —  Zerodha Auto-Auth Bot  —  CREDENTIALS TEMPLATE
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  HOW TO USE
#  ──────────
#  1. Copy this file:    cp .env.zerodha-bot.example .env
#     (Or merge these keys into your existing config/.env file.)
#  2. Fill in the 5 values below.
#  3. Restart the backend.  The auth_scheduler picks up env vars on boot
#     and self-arms — there is NO enable flag.
#  4. Verify with config/AUTH_BOT_SETUP.md (one-shot test).
#
#  SCHEDULE
#  ────────
#  The scheduler runs on a FIXED 4-cycle morning sequence:
#       06:30 / 07:30 / 08:30 / 09:00  IST  weekdays
#  Each cycle skips if the day already has a success row in
#  `falcon_auth_log`. On weekday restarts, a boot-catch-up runs the
#  latest passed cycle immediately so a daytime backend restart still
#  recovers the day. Weekends are skipped (market is closed).
#
#  This window targets the post-06:00-IST Zerodha token rollover; tokens
#  are good for the whole trading day once minted before 09:15 IST market
#  open.
#
#  SECURITY
#  ────────
#  • This file holds your Zerodha login. Treat it like a password.
#  • `config/.env` is gitignored. `config/.env.template` is NOT — never
#    paste real credentials into the template file.
#  • Credentials are read into env vars only; never written to the DB.
#  • Token audit-trail in `falcon_auth_log` only stores the first 8 chars
#    of the access token, not the full token.
#
#  WITHOUT THE 5 VALUES SET
#  ────────────────────────
#  The bot fires on schedule and logs `CONFIG_MISSING` rows in
#  `falcon_auth_log` (look for status='failed', error_code='CONFIG_MISSING').
#  Live signal endpoints (/api/power/picks/today, /live) keep serving the
#  most recent EOD batch, but live ticks and order placement won't work
#  until auth is healthy.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. KITE CONNECT APP CREDENTIALS ──────────────────────────────────────
# From your Kite Connect developer app at kite.trade/account/apps.

KITE_API_KEY=your_kite_api_key_here
KITE_API_SECRET=your_kite_api_secret_here


# ── 2. ZERODHA ACCOUNT LOGIN ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ZERODHA_USERNAME:  your Kite client ID, e.g. "AB1234"  (case-sensitive)
# ZERODHA_PASSWORD:  your Kite password (NOT your 2FA PIN — the actual password)
#                    NO leading or trailing spaces — strip them.

ZERODHA_USERNAME=your_client_id_here
ZERODHA_PASSWORD=your_zerodha_password_here


# ── 3. ZERODHA TOTP SECRET ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the **base32 SEED** that drives your authenticator app — NOT
# the rotating 6-digit code shown on screen.
#
# CRITICAL: your Zerodha account must be set to **TOTP** 2FA, NOT "Mobile
# App Code". Mobile App Code is unautomatable — codes only generate
# inside the Kite mobile app on your phone. If your account is on Mobile
# App Code, the bot will time out at the redirect step with the error
# "Invalid App Code". Switch to TOTP first: kite.zerodha.com → Profile →
# Settings → Password & Security → Reset 2FA → choose External TOTP
# (Google Authenticator / Authy / 1Password).
#
# How to extract the secret (one-time, ~2 minutes):
#   1. Log in to kite.zerodha.com → My Profile → Settings → Password & Security
#   2. Click "Reset/disable 2FA" → choose External TOTP → "Setup TOTP"
#   3. When the QR code appears, also click "Can't scan QR? Enter manually"
#   4. Zerodha shows a 16-32 character base32 string (uppercase A-Z + digits 2-7).
#      → THIS is your ZERODHA_TOTP_SECRET. Copy it BEFORE confirming.
#   5. Add the same secret to your authenticator app so you can still log
#      in manually if the bot is offline.
#   6. Confirm 2FA setup in Zerodha by entering the current 6-digit code.
#
# Pyotp turns this secret into the rotating 6-digit code automatically:
#   >>> import pyotp; pyotp.TOTP("FZBTYNZTOEYC2RJSHA5DSKBTGN3WGYRY").now()
#   '847532'   ← this is what the bot submits to the login form

ZERODHA_TOTP_SECRET=your_base32_totp_secret_here


# ── 4. KITE ACCESS TOKEN (populated by the bot — leave empty) ────────────
# Daily session token. The bot writes a fresh one to
# `data/db/kanida_quant.db.kite_tokens` after every successful login.
# No manual setting needed.

KITE_ACCESS_TOKEN=


# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  After filling these in, see  config/AUTH_BOT_SETUP.md  for:
#    • One-shot credential verification test
#    • Reading the audit trail in `falcon_auth_log`
#    • Failure-mode interpretation (BAD_CREDS / TOTP_FAILED / etc.)
#    • Manual refresh via the admin endpoint
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
